CORE
main.c
--allow-pointer-unsoundness --no-assertions --datarace --unwind 2 --rounds 2 --no-por
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
An address passed to __CPROVER_array_set does not make a local dirty (the
builtin keeps no pointer), but the same address passed to a thread does: the
thread writes a[0] through it while main sets the array, a race.
